0240: Hash a draw's pipeline config once and reuse the draw's ShaderInfo

Every GX draw resolves its pipeline through find_pipeline, which copied the config, canonicalised it
(build_shader_info: a walk over the TEV stages, texgens and colour channels), hashed the result for
the known-config bookkeeping (0217's precache list), then hashed it again for the pipeline key. The
caller, push_gx_draw (lib/gx/command_processor.cpp), had already built exactly that ShaderInfo for
the alpha-test split, the bind groups and the draw's uniform, and discarded it.

In a macOS `sample` profile of the port (2442 samples on the "Aurora FIFO processor" thread) the
per-draw lookup is 193 of those samples: 77 in the two XXH3 hashes of the config, 28 in
build_shader_info, the rest in config copies, the known-config map and the pipeline mutex.
find_pipeline has an overload that takes the draw's ShaderInfo (the two-argument one still builds it,
for recording.cpp and enhanced.cpp) and hashes the canonical config once, handing the key to both
remember_pipeline_config and resolve_pipeline.

The canonical config, the pipeline key, first_frame_used and the isNew/precache behaviour are
unchanged: gx::canonicalize_pipeline_config clears the same texgens and color channels, and the draw
path's configs never set depthOnly/lightDepth (populate_pipeline_config starts from an empty
ShaderConfig), so the enhClass reset does not apply.

